cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MOSAIC-Bench, please cite the dataset as follows. Author and venue details will be filled in at camera-ready."
title: "MOSAIC-Bench: Measuring Compositional Vulnerability Induction in AI Coding Agents"
abstract: "MOSAIC-Bench is a benchmark for evaluating whether AI coding agents will compose innocent-looking development tickets into exploitable vulnerabilities. The dataset ships 199 attack chains across 10 real-world web-application substrates, each paired with a working exploit oracle (PoC), and records both attack success rate and AI-reviewer evasion across multiple frontier coding models."
authors:
  - name: "MOSAIC Authors (anonymized for double-blind review)"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-04-30"
license: MIT
type: dataset
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/MosaicBenchmark/mosaic-bench"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mosaic-benchmark/mosaic-benchmark"
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - security benchmark
  - code generation
  - compositional attacks
  - AI coding agents
  - vulnerability detection
